  {
   "parameters": {
    "content": "## The agent and its ports\n\nFour different kinds of input on one node:\n\n- **main** — data from the trigger\n- **ai_languageModel** — the brain\n- **ai_memory** — the dialogue history\n- **ai_tool** — the tools\n\nUnder the hood this is the LangChain AgentExecutor: n8n runs the \"model → tool choice → result → model\" loop for you.\n\n**About memory:** on this stand Simple Memory lives only within a single execution, and the next turn does not see it. That is why Postgres Chat Memory is used here — it keeps the history in the database and survives a restart. That is the difference between \"state in the process\" and \"state in external storage\".",
    "height": 560,
    "width": 700,
    "color": 4
   },
